From aba41c7d653e7db85ae9b458fa4115861182fd0f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: FP mod <fpmod@localhost>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 20:34:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 08/27] Domain camera views: F4 cycles classic, high chase, low
 chase, first person

The camera moves smoothly between the views: height, distance, tilt, field of
view and rotation blend over 26 game frames, and the overhead view's squashed
tile rows unsquash on the way. The retail camera always runs and is read back
as the classic pose, so leaving and returning to classic is seamless. Controls
switch when a transition ends. Every dungeon rebuild (battle exit, new floor)
snaps to the chosen view. The beetle hides while the camera is within a tile
of it; solid cells get black wall-top caps seen from above, as retail draws
them; ceilings only with the eye below the walls. Setting domain_view 0..3.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01B1oHeiADE8njqFxkaQnJAX
